From 1bdb7e7a169b1b66ea0184577ea91357dd546017 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AOSP RK3576 Baseline <uhf-platform@localbuild>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 10:53:20 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 13/13] uhf: implement getInterfaceVersion/getInterfaceHash on
 the IUhfReaderCallback.Stub

Real compile error, found by actually running the build (not by
inspection) - the first time UhfHalTransport.java's anonymous
IUhfReaderCallback.Stub was compiled against the real generated AIDL
Java class rather than just checked by hand:

  UhfHalTransport.java:109: error: <anonymous
  com.android.server.uhf.UhfHalTransport$1> is not abstract and does not
  override abstract method getInterfaceHash() in IUhfReaderCallback

Confirmed against the actual generated
out/soong/.../rockchip.uhf.aidl-V1-java-source/gen/rockchip/uhf/aidl/IUhfReaderCallback.java:
Stub only supplies a body for onTransact()'s dispatch to
getInterfaceVersion()/getInterfaceHash() - it does not implement them
itself (only the separate IUhfReaderCallback.Default class does, which
this anonymous class doesn't extend). Every concrete Stub subclass has to
supply both. This isn't specific to our interface: real precedent in this
same tree, ThermalManagerService's own anonymous IThermalEventListener.Stub,
does exactly the same two-method override with the same
`return this.VERSION;` / `return this.HASH;` idiom.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../com/android/server/uhf/UhfHalTransport.java     | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/services/core/java/com/android/server/uhf/UhfHalTransport.java b/services/core/java/com/android/server/uhf/UhfHalTransport.java
index 9ab2889b..b0615bf2 100644
--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/uhf/UhfHalTransport.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/uhf/UhfHalTransport.java
@@ -125,6 +125,19 @@ final class UhfHalTransport implements UhfTransport {
                 mStreaming = false;
                 callback.onError(errorCode);
             }
+
+            // IUhfReaderCallback.Stub leaves these abstract (real AOSP precedent:
+            // ThermalManagerService's own anonymous IThermalEventListener.Stub does the same) -
+            // every concrete Stub subclass must supply them itself.
+            @Override
+            public int getInterfaceVersion() {
+                return IUhfReaderCallback.VERSION;
+            }
+
+            @Override
+            public String getInterfaceHash() {
+                return IUhfReaderCallback.HASH;
+            }
         };
         try {
             getHal().startStream(wrapper);
-- 
